_message() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> hid-logitech-hidpp is rebuilt for every 7.3-rc1 to 7.3-rc5 kernel with
    headers, but the running kernel keeps the module it loaded at boot.
    Reboot, or reload it:
      sudo modprobe -r hid_logitech_hidpp && sudo modprobe hid_logitech_hidpp
    then power-cycle the mouse once.
==> Kernel 7.3-rc6 and later do not have the bug and are not built for.
    Before booting one, turn off Scroll Wheel Diversion and Scroll Wheel
    Resolution, or the wheel stops scrolling there:
      solaar config "MX Master 4" hires-scroll-mode false
      solaar config "MX Master 4" hires-smooth-resolution false
    Remove this package once no 7.3-rc1 to 7.3-rc5 kernel is installed.
EOF
}

post_install() {
  _message
}

post_upgrade() {
  _message
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> The MX Master 4's wheel stays diverted to HID++ until something resets
    it, and the stock driver does not scroll from diverted events. Unless
    Solaar already has them off, turn off Scroll Wheel Diversion and Scroll
    Wheel Resolution, then reload the module while the mouse is awake:
      solaar config "MX Master 4" hires-scroll-mode false
      solaar config "MX Master 4" hires-smooth-resolution false
      sudo modprobe -r hid_logitech_hidpp && sudo modprobe hid_logitech_hidpp
EOF
}
